# Words the Clarity scripts use that cmudict-en-us does not carry.
# Alignment fails outright on an unknown word rather than skipping it, so every
# one has to be declared before the first window is decoded. Additive across
# scripts: declaring a word an audio file never says costs nothing.
# Pronunciations are the reading an English-language documentary voice gives
# them, not a transliteration standard — this file exists to let the acoustic
# search match the recording, nothing else.
